  <ferc:StatementAboutImportantChangesDuringTheQuarterYearTextBlock id="HHFF9F4E3640A578CDF5DE55A091A9A0F9" contextRef="HH6F430EA68AFC29D1DD829B0DDD45FFF4">&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="font-size: 14px;"&gt;&lt;span style="color: #495057; font-family: sans-serif;"&gt;1. Not Applicable&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br style="color: #495057; font-family: sans-serif;" /&gt;&lt;span style="color: #495057; font-family: sans-serif;"&gt;2. Not Applicable&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br style="color: #495057; font-family: sans-serif;" /&gt;&lt;span style="color: #495057; font-family: sans-serif;"&gt;3. Not Applicable&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br style="color: #495057; font-family: sans-serif;" /&gt;&lt;span style="color: #495057; font-family: sans-serif;"&gt;4. See Page 122 Notes to Financial Statements&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br style="color: #495057; font-family: sans-serif;" /&gt;&lt;span style="color: #495057; font-family: sans-serif;"&gt;5. Not Applicable&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="font-size: 14px;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:StatementAboutImportantChangesDuringTheQuarterYearTextBlock>
  <ferc:NotesToFinancialStatementsTextBlock id="HHFB845F6A13C048AB10E053139FD9FDD6" contextRef="HH6F430EA68AFC29D1DD829B0DDD45FFF4">&lt;div&gt;&#xD;
		&lt;div&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;p style="margin-top:0pt; margin-bottom:12pt; text-align:justify; font-size:10pt"&gt;&#xD;
				&lt;span style="font-family:Arial; font-weight:bold"&gt;NOTE A - ORGANIZATION, OPERATIONS AND BASIS OF PRESENTATION:&lt;/span&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;/p&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;p style="margin-top:0pt; margin-bottom:12pt; font-size:10.5pt"&gt;&#xD;
				&lt;span style="font-family:Arial; font-size:10pt; font-weight:bold"&gt;Organization&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial; font-size:10pt"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial; font-size:10pt"&gt;Mid Valley Pipeline Company LLC ("MVPL") is an indirect wholly owned subsidiary of Energy Transfer CC Holdings LLC. Energy Transfer CC Holdings LLC is a wholly owned subsidiary of Energy Transfer LP ("Energy Transfer").&lt;/span&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;/p&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;p style="margin-top:0pt; margin-bottom:12pt; font-size:10pt"&gt;&#xD;
				&lt;span style="font-family:Arial; font-weight:bold"&gt;Operations&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt;MVPL owns and operates a 1,060-mile crude oil pipeline from Longview, Texas and passes through Louisiana, Arkansas, Mississippi, Tennessee, Kentucky and Ohio and terminates in Samaria, Michigan. This pipeline provides crude oil to &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt;a number of&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt; refineries, primarily in the Midwest United States. MVPL &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt;owns&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt; an undivided interest (73.97%) in Maumee &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt;Pipe Line&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt; System.&lt;/span&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;/p&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;p style="margin-top:0pt; margin-bottom:12pt; text-align:justify; font-size:10pt"&gt;&#xD;
				&lt;span style="font-family:Arial; font-weight:bold"&gt;Regulation&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt;. MVPL's crude&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt;oil transportation activities are subject to regulation by the Federal Energy Regulatory Commission ("FERC") and various state authorities. Regulatory bodies exercise statutory authority over matters such as rates, underlying accounting practices, and rate-making agreements with customers.&lt;/span&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;/p&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;p style="margin-top:0pt; margin-bottom:12pt; font-size:10pt"&gt;&#xD;
				&lt;span style="font-family:Arial; font-weight:bold"&gt;Basis of Presentation&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt;The financial statements presented herein are prepared in accordance with the accounting requirements of the FERC, as set forth in the applicable Uniform System of Accounts and published accounting releases, which constitute a comprehensive basis of accounting other than accounting principles generally accepted in the United States of America ("GAAP").The most significant differences between GAAP and the financial statements presented herein are: (1) classification of certain accounts on the balance sheet, statement of income and the statement of cash flows and (2) use of FERC approved depreciation rates.&lt;/span&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;/p&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;p style="margin-top:0pt; margin-bottom:12pt; font-size:10pt"&gt;&#xD;
				&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt;These interim financial statements should be read in conjunction with the financial statements and notes thereto contained in the MVPL FERC Form 6 for the year ended December 31, 202&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt;5&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt;. The financial statements are unaudited, but in the opinion of management, all adjustments have been made that are necessary to fairly state the financial position, results of operations and cash flows for the periods presented. Certain information and notes that would substantially duplicate the disclosures contained in the most recent FERC Form 6 have been omitted.&lt;/span&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;/p&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;p style="margin-top:0pt; margin-bottom:12pt; text-align:justify; font-size:10pt"&gt;&#xD;
				&lt;span style="font-family:Arial; font-weight:bold"&gt;NOTE B -&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial; font-weight:bold"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial; font-weight:bold"&gt;COMMITMENTS, CONTINGENCIES AND ENVIRONMENTAL MATTERS:&lt;/span&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;/p&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;p style="margin-top:0pt; margin-bottom:0pt; font-size:10pt"&gt;&#xD;
				&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt;On October 13, 2023, MVPL received a Notice of Proposed Safety Order ("NOPSO") from the Pipeline and Hazardous Materials Safety Administration ("PHMSA") related to various historical accidents and complaints reported to PHMSA on the MVPL system. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt;The NOPSO&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt; requests that MVPL perform several proposed corrective measures within six months of receipt of a Safety Order; however, in response, MVPL requested that PHMSA engage in informal consultations prior to issuing a Safety Order in an effort for the parties to potentially enter into a Consent Agreement and Order. Informal consultation is underway. In the event a Consent Agreement and Order is not reached between the parties during this process, MVPL may request a Hearing on the NOPSO. The informal consultation process has concluded with PHMSA and MVPL reaching agreement on the Corrective Measures. PHMSA issued the Consent Agreement which was signed by MVPL on March 21, 2025. The fully executed version of the Consent Agreement was received by MVPL on April 24, 2025. All items required by the Consent Agreement have been completed and documentation, including the bi-annual report on the internal corrosion control program, submitted to PHMSA for review. MVPL met with PHMSA over the week of April 6, &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt;2026&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt; to review records related to the Consent Agreement and &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt;have completed&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt; a &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt;field inspection&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt; in the second quarter. MVPL is anticipating closure of the Consent Agreement in the third quarter of 2026.&lt;/span&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;/p&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;p style="margin-top:0pt; margin-bottom:0pt; font-size:10pt"&gt;&#xD;
				&lt;span style="font-family:Arial; "&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;/p&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;p style="margin-top:0pt; margin-bottom:12pt; text-align:justify; font-size:10pt"&gt;&#xD;
				&lt;span style="font-family:Arial; font-weight:bold"&gt;NOTE C - SUPPLEMENTAL CASH FLOW INFORMATION:&lt;/span&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;/p&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;p style="margin-top:0pt; margin-bottom:0pt; font-size:10pt"&gt;&#xD;
				&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt;Accrued capital &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt;expenditures as&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt; of &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt;June&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt; 3&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt;0&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt;, &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt;2026&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt; and 2025 were $&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt;1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt;4&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt; million and $0.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt;4&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt; million,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt; respectively.&lt;/span&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;/p&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;p style="margin-top:0pt; margin-bottom:0pt; font-size:10pt"&gt;&#xD;
				&lt;span style="font-family:Arial; "&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;/p&gt;&#xD;
		&lt;/div&gt;&#xD;
	&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:NotesToFinancialStatementsTextBlock>
  <ferc:DisclosureOfEventsThatHaveAMaterialEffectToRespondentsTextBlock id="HH11476EB422E065C84DE3B12A8533C405" contextRef="HH6F430EA68AFC29D1DD829B0DDD45FFF4"></ferc:DisclosureOfEventsThatHaveAMaterialEffectToRespondentsTextBlock>
